Modbus Read/Write debug window (.NET 10 / Windows Forms)

Open ModbusReadWrite/ModbusReadWrite.slnx in Visual Studio with .NET 10 SDK.
Restore NuGet packages (System.IO.Ports 10.0.0), then build and run.

COM ports refresh every second. Connect/disconnect releases the port; removing
an active port disconnects automatically. Baud: 4800..230400. UART formats:
7/8 bits, N/E/O parity, 1/2 stop bits. RTU requires 8 bits. ASCII supports 7/8.
Station is decimal 1..247, default 2. Protocol defaults to RTU, UART to 115200 8/N/1.

Each of the 13 rows reads ONE holding register with 03 or writes ONE register
with 06. Addresses are zero-based protocol addresses, not 4xxxx references.
Checked HEX accepts 1010h, 0x1010, or 1010. Unchecked DEC accepts 0..65535.
The row checkbox applies to both address and value and converts both without
changing their numerical value. Registers are unsigned 16-bit values.

RX validates station, function, CRC/LRC, length, exception responses and 06 echo.
Commands run off the UI thread and are serialized; timeout is one second.
TX/RX log displays decoded Modbus payloads (without framing/checksum).
No automatic retry of writes. A timed-out write may already have reached the
slave: read back before deciding whether to repeat it.

Validation environment had no .NET SDK or serial hardware. Windows build,
USB hotplug, RTU/ASCII reads/writes and exception responses need live validation.
